WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.996 --> 00:00:14.899
Brad: But, Danny, how is a candle going to help?

2
00:00:14.919 --> 00:00:16.620
Danny: What do you mean?

3
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.640
Brad: It’s not lit.

4
00:00:19.101 --> 00:00:20.321
How are we going to light it?

5
00:00:20.341 --> 00:00:24.182
Danny: What if I make a flame out of yellow clay?

6
00:00:24.202 --> 00:00:26.322
Tina: Try it, Danny!

7
00:00:26.342 --> 00:00:27.683
Danny: Okay.

8
00:00:27.863 --> 00:00:29.823
Tina, you hold the candle for me.

9
00:00:29.843 --> 00:00:31.764
Tina: Don’t take too long.

10
00:00:32.888 --> 00:00:34.409
Danny: There!

11
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:42.631
I-I t-told y-you it wouldn’t w-w-work.

12
00:00:43.331 --> 00:00:46.292
Danny: Yes, it will.

13
00:00:46.592 --> 00:00:48.232
We just have to concentrate.

14
00:00:48.252 --> 00:00:50.573
Danny: Imagine that the flame is burning.

15
00:00:50.593 --> 00:00:53.074
Danny: That’s how we made the doors appear.

16
00:00:53.094 --> 00:00:56.355
Tina: And how we escaped from the squishy soil.

17
00:00:57.555 --> 00:00:58.235
Brad: Okay.

18
00:00:58.275 --> 00:00:59.075
Let’s try.

19
00:00:59.095 --> 00:01:01.416
I don’t want to freeze again!

20
00:01:02.956 --> 00:01:05.237
Danny: Concentrate really hard.

21
00:01:05.577 --> 00:01:06.598
Ready? Go!

22
00:01:06.618 --> 00:01:14.401
Danny: Awesome!

23
00:01:14.661 --> 00:01:15.361
We did it!

24
00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.182
Tina: Let’s hope it’s hot enough to melt this snow!

25
00:01:18.202 --> 00:01:21.064
Brad: That’s a pretty small flame.

26
00:01:21.084 --> 00:01:24.485
Danny: Just give it a minute.

27
00:01:24.505 --> 00:01:26.866
Tina: It’s not helping much.

28
00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.007
Danny: But we have fire.

29
00:01:29.327 --> 00:01:30.888
We must be able to use it.

30
00:01:32.524 --> 00:01:33.985
Brad: Just give me one minute.

31
00:01:36.786 --> 00:01:38.126
Brad: Here, I found it!

32
00:01:38.146 --> 00:01:41.888
Brad: Danny, help me gather some flat shiny pieces of ice.

33
00:01:41.908 --> 00:01:43.529
Danny: Why?

34
00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:45.590
Brad: I’ll show you.

35
00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:48.031
Pass me that piece by your foot there.

36
00:01:48.051 --> 00:01:49.091
Brad: Thanks.

37
00:01:49.491 --> 00:01:51.232
I just need five or six pieces.

38
00:01:51.252 --> 00:01:55.394
Tina: Whatever you’re doing, Brad, do it quickly.

39
00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:58.015
Tina: My arm is beginning to ice up again!

40
00:01:58.035 --> 00:02:00.436
Brad: I’m making a curved mirror.

41
00:02:01.152 --> 00:02:03.194
Brad: I found instructions on my computer.

42
00:02:03.214 --> 00:02:06.897
Brad: We just place the ice in a circle, like this.

43
00:02:06.917 --> 00:02:10.880
Brad: Then lean the pieces at a 45-degree angle.

44
00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:15.183
There! Brad: Now place the candle in the center, Tina.

45
00:02:15.203 --> 00:02:18.106
Danny: Let’s hope this works!

46
00:02:20.888 --> 00:02:22.649
Tina: Look, the roof is melting.

47
00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:30.476
I’m feeling warmer already!

48
00:02:31.188 --> 00:02:33.609
Danny: Look how fast the snow is melting now!

49
00:02:33.629 --> 00:02:37.772
Tina: Hey, Danny!

50
00:02:38.152 --> 00:02:39.532
Doesn’t that look like a leaf?

51
00:02:39.773 --> 00:02:40.773
Danny: Yes!

52
00:02:41.313 --> 00:02:43.054
And there’s a flower over there!

53
00:02:43.074 --> 00:02:49.338
Danny: This is so cool!

54
00:02:49.798 --> 00:02:51.439
There are hundreds of flowers.

55
00:02:51.459 --> 00:02:54.661
Brad: I wonder what kind of world this is.

56
00:02:54.681 --> 00:02:57.582
Tina: I hope it’s the giants’ world.

57
00:02:58.182 --> 00:03:00.684
If it isn’t, it’s probably dangerous.

58
00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.383
Danny: Well, let’s find out if it is the giants’ world.

59
00:03:05.403 --> 00:03:09.087
Danny: Hopian?

60
00:03:09.107 --> 00:03:13.631
Tina: Danny, I don’t see any giants wandering around.

61
00:03:13.651 --> 00:03:16.133
Brad: Maybe there’s a clue somewhere.

62
00:03:16.153 --> 00:03:18.555
Tina: Let’s go explore.
